  "term": "lPOA",
  "definition": "LPOA refers to a linear programming optimization algorithm used in assessment to combine several initial indicator weights into a final set of weights, here within confidence intervals estimated from a t-distribution. In this use, it is intended to reduce overemphasis on any single indicator in a multi-factor risk assessment.",
